From c3f527541da470dc6128eb992fa786ac59d837ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Drive Player <drive-player@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:43:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec: lend pictures read-only so that a decoder draws over
 a copy

A decoder that draws each frame over its last (FlashSV, QuickTime RLE,
RPZA, Microsoft RLE and Video 1, FLIC and others) takes its last frame
again for the next one, and draws in place when FFmpeg finds its buffer
writable. With direct rendering, that buffer is a picture lent to the
decoder, and the picture the decoder output, a clone sharing its planes,
waits in the video output to be shown. No reference of FFmpeg's but the
decoder's held the buffer, so FFmpeg found it writable and the next
frames were drawn over the picture waiting. A picture then showed the
last frame decoded, as far ahead as the decoding runs ahead of the
display, not its own: after a seek, an input showed frames ahead of its
time.

Lend the picture's planes read-only. Such a decoder then takes a new
picture and copies its last frame into it before drawing, as a frame is
copied out without direct rendering; the other decoders take a new
buffer for each frame and do not ask whether it is writable.
---
 modules/codec/avcodec/video.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/codec/avcodec/video.c b/modules/codec/avcodec/video.c
index f6925b9..0d97854 100644
--- a/modules/codec/avcodec/video.c
+++ b/modules/codec/avcodec/video.c
@@ -1689,8 +1689,12 @@ static int lavc_dr_GetFrame(struct AVCodecContext *ctx, AVFrame *frame,
 
         frame->data[i] = data;
         frame->linesize[i] = pic->p[i].i_pitch;
+        /* The picture goes out as soon as it is decoded, while the decoder may
+         * keep it as its last frame. One that draws each frame over its last
+         * (FlashSV, QuickTime RLE, Microsoft RLE...) would draw over a picture
+         * waiting to be shown: lent read-only, it draws over a copy. */
         frame->buf[i] = av_buffer_create(data, size, lavc_ReleaseFrame,
-                                         pic, 0);
+                                         pic, AV_BUFFER_FLAG_READONLY);
         if (unlikely(frame->buf[i] == NULL))
         {
             while (i > 0)
